# A dialog over a page held still: the body fixed to the viewport and clipped,
# a fixed backdrop over everything, the dialog fixed INSIDE the backdrop — the
# way a consent dialog is written. The dialog is laid out at all (a fixed box
# met while another fixed box is being placed), is drawn over its backdrop
# (it is kept under the stacking context it was written in), can be pressed,
# and the page scrolls again once it has gone. And a fixed box inside a box
# that clips is clipped by the viewport alone.
resize 800 600
open modal.html
assert-title Modal
# The page under the backdrop: its blue, half darkened.
assert-pixel 40 400 #666e77
# The dialog, white, in the middle of the window — over the backdrop.
assert-pixel 400 300 #ffffff
assert-text Accept
# The fixed box written inside the clipping card: all of it shows, darkened
# by the backdrop like everything else, far outside the card's 200 by 60.
assert-pixel 310 200 #551919
assert-pixel 410 120 #551919
# Held still: the wheel moves nothing.
wheel -3
assert-scroll 0
# A press on the dialog's link reaches it, and lets the page go.
click-text Accept
assert-title Unlocked
assert-pixel 40 400 #ccddee
assert-no-text Accept
wheel -3
assert-scroll 180
# The fixed box can be pressed where it shows, outside the card it is kept in.
click 360 160
assert-title Tip
